@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Deploying Applications on Azure";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Deploying applications on Azure ensures scalability, security, and high availability. Azure provides multiple deployment options, including App Services, Virtual Machines, Kubernetes, and serverless solutions.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Deploy on Azure?</h2>
        <p>Azure offers a robust cloud platform for application deployment with several benefits:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Automatically scale applications based on demand.</li>
            <li><strong>High Availability:</strong> Deploy applications across multiple regions for redundancy.</li>
            <li><strong>Security & Compliance:</strong> Built-in security controls and compliance with industry standards.</li>
            <li><strong>Cost Optimization:</strong> Pay-as-you-go pricing and reserved instances for cost savings.</li>
            <li><strong>Managed Services:</strong> Reduce operational overhead with fully managed solutions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-app-deployment.png" alt="Azure Deployment Options" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Deployment Options</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Azure Deployment Options</h2>
        <p>Azure provides various deployment solutions depending on the application architecture and requirements:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Azure App Services:</strong> Best for web applications, APIs, and mobile backends.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Virtual Machines (VMs):</strong> Full control over infrastructure for complex applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS):</strong> Containerized application deployment and orchestration.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Functions:</strong> Serverless computing for event-driven applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Azure Logic Apps:</strong> Low-code workflow automation and integration.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Steps to Deploy an Application on Azure</h2>
        <p>Follow these key steps to deploy an application on Azure:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Set Up an Azure Subscription:</strong> Create an Azure account and configure billing.</li>
            <li><strong>Choose a Deployment Service:</strong> Select App Services, VMs, AKS, or Functions based on requirements.</li>
            <li><strong>Prepare the Application:</strong> Ensure the application is containerized or packaged properly.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure CI/CD Pipeline:</strong> Automate deployment using Azure DevOps.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor & Optimize:</strong> Use Azure Monitor, Application Insights, and Log Analytics.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Security & Scaling:</strong> Apply RBAC, network security, and autoscaling strategies.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Deploying to Azure App Service</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
stages:
- stage: Deploy
  jobs:
  - job: DeployApp
    steps:
    - task: AzureWebApp@1
      inputs:
        azureSubscription: 'MyAzureSubscription'
        appName: 'MyWebApp'
        package: '$(Build.ArtifactStagingDirectory)/drop.zip'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Azure Deployment</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Use Infrastructure as Code (IaC):</strong> Automate deployments with Terraform or ARM templates.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable Auto-Scaling:</strong> Configure auto-scaling to handle workload fluctuations.</li>
            <li><strong>Secure Deployments:</strong> Implement RBAC, Azure Policy, and private endpoints.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor Performance:</strong> Use Application Insights for real-time monitoring.</li>
            <li><strong>Implement Backup & Disaster Recovery:</strong> Regularly back up data and enable failover strategies.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>Deploying applications on Azure allows organizations to build, scale, and manage cloud-native applications efficiently. A well-configured deployment strategy ensures performance, security, and cost-effectiveness.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("EndToEndCICD", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Setting Up End-to-End CI/CD Pipeline</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("TroubleshootDebug", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Troubleshooting & Debugging in Azure &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>